From: Sweet port <sweet@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mig: match the kernel-side exception-port prototypes GNU mig generates

osfmk/kern/task.h and osfmk/kern/thread.h declare the kernel-side
prototypes for the MIG-generated task_get_exception_ports /
thread_get_exception_ports. Those declarations were written against
Apple's mig and no longer agree with what GNU mig emits, so every
translation unit that sees both dies with

    task.h:1225:22: error: conflicting types for 'task_get_exception_ports'
    ../mach/task.h:206:15: note: previous declaration is here

139 times each in run 40419596108 -- 278 of the run's 582 errors, the
single largest remaining group.

THE DIFFERENCE IS THE COUNT PARAMETERS, NOT THE TYPES

Apple's mig implements `SameCount` by having several out-parameters share
one count. Its generated prototype therefore carries a single count:

    (task_t, exception_mask_t, exception_mask_array_t masks,
     mach_msg_type_number_t *CountCnt, exception_port_array_t ports,
     exception_behavior_array_t behaviors,
     thread_state_flavor_array_t flavors)                       /* 7 */

GNU mig has no `SameCount` syntax at all (nothing in parser.y mentions a
count binding), so each out-array gets its own trailing count pointer:

    (task_t, exception_mask_t, exception_mask_array_t masks,
     mach_msg_type_number_t *masksCnt,
     mach_msg_type_number_t *CountCnt,
     exception_handler_array_t old_handlers,
     mach_msg_type_number_t *old_handlersCnt,
     exception_behavior_array_t old_behaviors,
     mach_msg_type_number_t *old_behaviorsCnt,
     exception_flavor_array_t old_flavors,
     mach_msg_type_number_t *old_flavorsCnt)                    /* 9 */

The appended `*CountCnt` came from this port's own migcom shim, which
rewrites `SameCount` into an explicit `out CountCnt : mach_msg_type_number_t`
so the stream parses at all. The other four count pointers are GNU mig's
own doing.

THE TYPES WERE NEVER THE PROBLEM

Checked rather than assumed, because a wrong diagnosis here would have
sent me rewriting typedefs that are already equivalent:

    mach_types.h:223   typedef mach_port_t exception_handler_t;
    mach_types.h:224   typedef exception_handler_t *exception_handler_array_t;
    exception_types.h:210  typedef mach_port_t *exception_port_array_t;
    thread_status.h:94/95  typedef int thread_state_flavor_t;
                           typedef thread_state_flavor_t *thread_state_flavor_array_t;
    exception_types.h:209  typedef thread_state_flavor_t *exception_flavor_array_t;

All of them bottom out in `mach_port_t *` or `int *`, so
exception_handler_array_t == exception_port_array_t and
exception_flavor_array_t == thread_state_flavor_array_t as types. Only
the arity differs, which is why this is an edit to the prototype rather
than to any header's typedefs.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES

Rewrites the two declarations to the GNU signature. Nothing else. The
arrays keep the names the generated code uses so the call sites read the
same, and the extra counts are what GNU mig's server implementations
already expect.

Scope: two functions. `SameCount` appears 24 times across host_priv.defs,
task.defs and thread_act.defs, but only these two routines have a
hand-written kernel prototype that has to agree with the generated one;
the rest are consumed through the generated header alone.

This is a port artefact, not an upstream bug: upstream is self-consistent
with Apple's mig. It belongs with the migcom shim rather than in the tree.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/task.h b/osfmk/kern/task.h
--- a/osfmk/kern/task.h
+++ b/osfmk/kern/task.h
@@ -1225,10 +1225,14 @@ extern boolean_t kdp_task_is_locked(task_t task);
 /* Kernel side prototypes for MIG routines */
 extern kern_return_t task_get_exception_ports(
 	task_t                          task,
 	exception_mask_t                exception_mask,
 	exception_mask_array_t          masks,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *masksCnt,
 	mach_msg_type_number_t          *CountCnt,
-	exception_port_array_t          ports,
-	exception_behavior_array_t      behaviors,
-	thread_state_flavor_array_t     flavors);
+	exception_handler_array_t       old_handlers,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *old_handlersCnt,
+	exception_behavior_array_t      old_behaviors,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *old_behaviorsCnt,
+	exception_flavor_array_t        old_flavors,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *old_flavorsCnt);
 
 #endif  /* XNU_KERNEL_PRIVATE */
 #ifdef  KERNEL_PRIVATE
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/thread.h b/osfmk/kern/thread.h
--- a/osfmk/kern/thread.h
+++ b/osfmk/kern/thread.h
@@ -1728,10 +1728,14 @@ extern kern_return_t thread_get_exception_ports(
 	thread_t                        thread,
 	exception_mask_t                exception_mask,
 	exception_mask_array_t          masks,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *masksCnt,
 	mach_msg_type_number_t          *CountCnt,
-	exception_port_array_t          ports,
-	exception_behavior_array_t      behaviors,
-	thread_state_flavor_array_t     flavors);
+	exception_handler_array_t       old_handlers,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *old_handlersCnt,
+	exception_behavior_array_t      old_behaviors,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *old_behaviorsCnt,
+	exception_flavor_array_t        old_flavors,
+	mach_msg_type_number_t          *old_flavorsCnt);
 
 extern kern_return_t thread_get_special_port(
 	thread_inspect_t         thread,
